  "design_rationale": "First-order self-draining heater: y_ss(u)=y_amb+K*u with y_amb~0.08, K~1.1, tau~150-175s from E1-E5 fits. Hold for 0.5 is (0.5-0.08)/1.1~0.38. Open-loop tau alone needs >350s to settle from cold, so need boosted heating then back-off. P-only with feedforward gives fast first-order approach with time constant tau/(1+K*Kp)~60-70s and no overshoot; integral is only needed to trim feedforward error. Therefore feedforward 0.38 + Kp*e + conditional integral, filtered y, output clamped to [0,0.70] so even stuck-high steady is 0.83<0.85 soft limit, integral limited to +-0.30 to cover >0.2 feedforward error without windup, integration frozen when |e|>0.12 or when saturated in direction of error to prevent heat-up windup and overshoot that evaluator scores on true state.",
